# One site's secrets: copy to .kamal/secrets.<site> (not committed). Each line
# reads the value from the environment, a file or a password manager; never
# write a raw value here.
#
# A new site gets its own (bin/rails secret; ruby -rsecurerandom -e 'puts SecureRandom.alphanumeric(32)').
# A site moved from the old shared install sets only SECRET_KEY_BASE, to the
# old install's, or its encrypted API tokens and integration keys become
# unreadable.
SECRET_KEY_BASE=$EXAMPLE_SITE_SECRET_KEY_BASE
AR_ENCRYPTION_PRIMARY_KEY=$EXAMPLE_SITE_AR_ENCRYPTION_PRIMARY_KEY
AR_ENCRYPTION_DETERMINISTIC_KEY=$EXAMPLE_SITE_AR_ENCRYPTION_DETERMINISTIC_KEY
AR_ENCRYPTION_KEY_DERIVATION_SALT=$EXAMPLE_SITE_AR_ENCRYPTION_KEY_DERIVATION_SALT
# SMTP_PASSWORD=$OUTSEND_API_KEY

# The install's plugins, overriding the empty default in secrets-common:
# CMS_PLUGINS="https://github.com/org/cms-seo#v1.2.0"
